recondition that RHAISTRAT-9990 has landed and its schema is final.\n  If the final schema matches the draft, this epic shrinks to verification; if it\n  differs, the isolation layer absorbs the change inside the reporting backend.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n  Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and NFRs are absent. Teams and ACs were\n  inferred from HLRs and architecture context; a human should confirm team\n  ownership, in particular the inferred documentation owner (Distributed\n  Workloads) and the inferred placement of the report API in Distributed\n  Workloads rather than the Dashboard.\n- **External timing risk (the strategy's open question)**: the metering data\n  schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. Mitigated by the Tier 1/Tier 2\n  split and the schema-isolation layer; the residual risk is rework in E003 if\n  the final schema diverges materially from the draft. E003's start date is\n  externally controlled and cannot be compressed by this strategy.\n- **Priority notes**: E003 is P0 because it completes HLR-1 (P0) in final form,\n  even though it is Tier 2 and gated on external timing — planners should not\n  read its P0 as \"start immediately\". E004 is P1 (docs-authoring exception:\n  strategy priority Major → P1), which is higher than HLR-4's P2 label; this is\n  the rule-mandated derivation, not a priority inversion.\n- **Scope boundary enforced as AC**: the metering collection pipeline\n  (RHAISTRAT-9990) is out of scope; E001 carries an explicit AC that metering is\n  consumed, not re-implemented.\n- No epic exceeds the ~2-week guideline; no re-split triggers required.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31215,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf8e95f1ec8b3de1","agent_id":"a4a18bdb468808aca","session_id":"1ce7f518-86cd-4dc0-977d-8d36a0eb367d","uuid":"7d