{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b54f03eb85b039","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU-hour chargeback reporting backend (Tier 1)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project GPU-hour chargeback reporting backend (Tier 1)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the reporting backend for administrator-facing GPU chargeback:\n34\tcomputation of per-project GPU-hour consumption aggregates over selectable time\n35\tranges from the metering data delivered by the in-flight GPU usage metering work\n36\t(RHAISTRAT-9990), exposed through a stable report retrieval API with CSV export\n37\tfor finance tooling. A schema-isolation layer confines every reference to the\n38\tmetering data schema so that schema changes from the in-flight metering strategy\n39\tare absorbed in one place. Metering collection itself is consumed, never\n40\tre-implemented. This is Tier 1 work: it builds against the current draft metering\n41\tschema behind the isolation layer so it does not wait for the metering strategy\n42\tto land.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Report computation producing per-project GPU-hour consumption aggregates over\n47\t  selectable time ranges, sourced from the metering data delivered by\n48\t  RHAISTRAT-9990.\n49\t- A schema-isolation layer that confines all metering-schema references\n50\t  (mappings from metering data fields to the report model), validated against\n51\t  the current draft schema.\n52\t- A stable report retrieval API suitable for programmatic consumers such as\n53\t  finance tooling.\n54\t- CSV export of the same report data.\n55\t- Report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) applied consistently with the\n56\t  metering data's semantics.\n57\t\n58\tOut of scope: the metering collection pipeline (RHAISTRAT-9990) and\n59\tcurrency/cost-rate modelling — reports are in GPU-hours, not dollars.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given metering data, per-project GPU-hour consumption aggregates are computable\n64\t  for selectable time ranges, and the metering data is consumed rather than\n65\t  re-implemented (no collection-side pipeline code is added).\n66\t- All references to the metering data schema are confined to the isolation layer,\n67\t  verified by a structural check or test; the layer is validated against the\n68\t  current draft schema.\n69\t- Reports are retrievable as CSV and via the stable report API by a non-UI\n70\t  client.\n71\t- Aggregate outputs are deterministic and reproducible for a fixed time range and\n72\t  fixed input data, verified by a test with fixture data.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n77\t  ranges — computation and retrieval portion.\n78\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API for finance tooling — bundled\n79\t  with HLR-1 because it is a presentation mode of the same report data surface\n80\t  and API, for the same component and team; splitting would build the same\n81\t  surface twice.\n82\t\n83\t## Risks / Notes\n84\t\n85\t- The metering data schema is not final until RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; the\n86\t  isolation layer is the containment for that risk, and final-schema alignment\n87\t  is deferred to dedicated follow-on work gated on that strategy landing.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e70839a58d64d1","agent_id":"a1d62a9cc75a4342b","session_id":"1ce7f518-86cd-4dc0-977d-8d36a0eb367d","uuid":"46f258d1-d9c0-47f9-a02b-f4a312334bd1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:13:27.479Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b54f03eb85b039","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
