line itself, and\n51\tcurrency/cost-rate modelling.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Reports compute correctly against the final metering data schema, with the\n56\t  isolation layer updated or removed accordingly.\n57\t- Report outputs (view data, CSV, API) are verified for consistency against\n58\t  delivered metering data.\n59\t- No references to superseded draft-schema constructs remain outside the\n60\t  isolation layer, verified by a structural check or test.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports — final-form computation\n65\t  against the delivered metering data schema.\n66\t\n67\t## Risks / Notes\n68\t\n69\t- Start is gated by an external precondition: RHAISTRAT-9990 must land and its\n70\t  data schema be final. That timing is controlled by the metering strategy and\n71\t  cannot be compressed here; it is a scheduling precondition, not an acceptance\n72\t  criterion. If the final schema differs materially from the draft, the\n73\t  isolation layer absorbs the change within the reporting backend.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1e70839a58d64d1","agent_id":"a1d62a9cc75a4342b","session_id":"1ce7f518-86cd-4dc0-977d-8d36a0eb367d","uuid":"8be2f622-06af-4cc2-9382-e07370ff30e0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:13:29.484Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a4b961a40b65d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
